SUMMARY:Ithaca College presents The Fidelio Trio - Music of Friends
DTSTART:20261022T230000Z
DTEND:20261023T035959Z
DTSTAMP:20261010T152037Z
UID:1fbf0d36b761961af7f76d8c120bcd2ce40dabbf@corning-events
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Music
DESCRIPTION:Darragh Morgan\, violin\nTim Gill\, cello\nMary Dullea\, piano
 \nThursday\, October 22\, 2026\n7PM | Hockett Family Recital Hall at Ithac
 a College\n953 Danby Road\, Ithaca\, NY\n'The virtuosic Fidelio Trio' (Sun
 day Times London) return to Ithaca College following their inaugural 2024 
 visit. Renowned exponents of new music -'They make what they do look all t
 oo effortless' (San Francisco Classical Voice) - Fidelio Trio have recorde
 d over 40 albums\, winning Gramophone Album of the Year and working closel
 y with leading composers such as Philip Glass\, Anna Clyne\, John Harbison
 . Their regular US visits include performances at National Sawdust New Yor
 k\, Andy Warhol Museum Pittsburgh\, Morrison Artists Series San Francisco 
 with masterclass invitations to Peabody Conservatory\, Curtis Institute an
 d MIT.\nThis special Ithaca College programme includes Bulb by Princeton P
 rofessor Donnacha Dennehy\, a Fidelio Trio commission which they have perf
 ormed on over 50 occasions\, a world premiere by University of Iowa Profes
 sor David Gompper with whom the trio have a long artistic association\, ne
 w music by Columbia University Professor George Lewis\, Ithaca's own Profe
 ssor Jorge Grossmann and a stunning arrangement of Debussy's La Mer for pi
 ano trio by British composer\, Sally Beamish.\nReserve your FREE tickets h
 ere:\nhttps://www.purplepass.com/events/388755-fidelio-trio-oct-22nd-2026
 \n\nSource: FLXcalendar - https://calendar.time.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78487023
 /20261022190000
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://calendar.time.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78487023/20261022190000
END:VEVENT
