BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Book Launch: Beyond Dreamers w/ Sofya Aptekar & Shannon Gleeson
DTSTART:20261030T213000Z
DTEND:20261031T035959Z
DTSTAMP:20261010T152037Z
UID:03157cad8eabcd8683955566d35e5d023e744cc7@corning-events
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:History & Heritage,Literature
DESCRIPTION:Beyond Dreamers: Transitions to Adulthood in an Uncertain Age
 \nJoin Sofya Aptekar and Shannon Gleeson for a conversation on Beyond Drea
 mers: Transitions to Adulthood in an Uncertain Age. Beyond Dreamers deftly
  underscores how deeply legal uncertainty continues to structure the lives
  of undocumented young adults.\nDrawing on more than one hundred interview
 s with a racially and ethnically diverse group of undocumented college stu
 dents in New York City\, with and without DACA authorization\, Aptekar and
  Hsin show that there is no single undocumented experience. They find that
  while legal status matters enormously\, its impacts are influenced by rac
 e\, national origin\, gender\, class\, sexuality\, family resources\, educ
 ational institutions\, neighborhood contexts\, and access to local and tra
 nsnational co-ethnic communities and labor markets. These forces not only 
 shape the kinds of opportunities available to undocumented young adults\, 
 but how they choose to approach disclosing their undocumented status and i
 nteract with family\, peers\, employers\, professors\, and police.\n\nSour
 ce: FLXcalendar - https://calendar.time.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78480759/2026103
 0173000
GEO:42.441218;-76.498352
LOCATION:Buffalo Street Books\, 215 North Cayuga Street\, Ithaca\, New Yor
 k\, 14850\, United States
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://calendar.time.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78480759/20261030173000
END:VEVENT
